WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:05.940
Adjacent to known reality lies an&nbsp;
infinite abyss of liminal spaces and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:11.700
monstrous beings - The Backrooms. As with&nbsp;
all unusual and supernatural phenomena,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:18.240
The SCP Foundation was set on cataloging the&nbsp;
Backrooms as an anomaly and finding a way to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:24.540
contain it. But unfortunately, all it took was&nbsp;
one failed experiment for the opposite to occur.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:39.100
Adjacent to known reality lies an infinite&nbsp;
abyss of liminal spaces and monstrous beings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:39.401
- The Backrooms. As with all unusual and&nbsp;
supernatural phenomena, The SCP Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.401 --> 00:00:40.260
was set on cataloging the Backrooms as an&nbsp;
anomaly and finding a way to contain it. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:55.680
unfortunately, all it took was one failed&nbsp;
experiment for the opposite to occur.&nbsp;

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:16.260
Sprinting through the maze towards the&nbsp;
smiler, SCP-096 was quickly too far away&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:22.860
for the Foundation staff to attempt recapture.&nbsp;
Moreover, this situation demanded a far more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:28.440
immediate concern - there was no apparent&nbsp;
way to no-clip the lost portions of the site&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:34.740
back to native reality. The researchers,&nbsp;
D-class, and MTF personnel who were now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:40.200
on the other side would have to adapt and&nbsp;
fend for themselves in this new reality.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.520
Agent Cullen, the highest-ranked member&nbsp;
of the mobile task force present,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:48.300
identified several hostile&nbsp;
entities approaching. These&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:52.680
bundles of arms were known as Clumps,&nbsp;
and since they did not possess eyes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.680 --> 00:02:00.060
they had evaded 096’s wrathful response to&nbsp;
entities that saw its face. On Cullen’s orders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:05.160
the researchers and D-class took cover behind&nbsp;
the agents, who opened fire on the Clumps.&nbsp;

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:12.000
Meanwhile, SCP-096 caught up to the Smiler that&nbsp;
had glimpsed its face. In most cases, Smilers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:17.100
are highly dangerous entities that prey on humans&nbsp;
who are trapped in the backrooms by pulling them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:24.240
into the shadows. Because this was its nature,&nbsp;
the smiler was not prepared for 096 to not only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:30.000
approach at top speed but to deliver a slamming&nbsp;
arm thrust straight into the creature’s face.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.380
The smiler instantly knew that one more&nbsp;
blow like that would be the destruction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:38.940
of its strange monstrous existence,&nbsp;
but it was too late to get away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:46.560
and 096 certainly didn’t stop at one. After&nbsp;
beating the smiler to a pulp, SCP-096 briefly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:51.600
returned to a more neutral state of being. It&nbsp;
was not at all fazed by the new surroundings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:57.060
in fact, it was temporarily relieved&nbsp;
by the solitude of the Backrooms maze.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:03:03.900
That was when SCP-096 felt the gaze of something&nbsp;
unknowably powerful staring at it from deeper&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:10.500
within the Backrooms dimensions. SCP-096 was no&nbsp;
stranger to being remotely viewed and becoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:17.580
enraged by it, but this was different. These&nbsp;
eyes were everywhere and nowhere all at once.

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:24.060
096 felt like it was being torn apart by its&nbsp;
own violent impulse to destroy whatever entity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:30.900
was currently seeing its face. With no clear&nbsp;
target present, SCP-096 dropped to all fours,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:36.840
and in an instant, it ran like a mad beast&nbsp;
through every conceivable corridor of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:42.720
infinite yellow maze in less than a single&nbsp;
second. During this blindingly fast rampage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:47.760
096 found itself back near the Foundation&nbsp;
personnel for a fraction of a moment.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:52.380
None of the humans present could perceive the&nbsp;
shy guy at the hypersonic speed it was going,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:58.320
but the result of it passing by was evident in&nbsp;
the abrupt death of several MTF agents who were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:05.100
still focused on fending off the clumps. It was&nbsp;
collateral damage to 096, who didn’t intend for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:10.680
its speeding body to collide with the agents, but&nbsp;
in any case, the clumps were at that much more of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:15.780
an advantage when it came to brutally attacking&nbsp;
the members of the research team. The clumps'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:21.000
numbers were increasing as well, as more of the&nbsp;
fleshy aberrations rolled forth from the woodwork.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:27.900
One of the D-Class - D-3461 - panicked, breaking&nbsp;
away from the defensive line and bludgeoning an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:32.700
MTF agent from behind. The others were still&nbsp;
reeling from the sudden slaughter created by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:38.820
SCP-096, and were not quick enough to stop&nbsp;
D-3462 from turning tail and running off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:44.520
into the maze with a stolen Mobile Task Force&nbsp;
issue firearm. The clumps seemed to ignore&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:50.580
this and focused on the larger group of humans&nbsp;
present, closing in well… a clump of clumps.

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:55.560
Senior researcher Dr. Hart - an expert&nbsp;
in reading the body language of anomalous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.560 --> 00:05:00.720
creatures - noticed this idiosyncratic movement&nbsp;
immediately. She immediately notified the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:05.100
rest of the research team that the clumps&nbsp;
seemed to prioritize going after humans in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:10.920
groups. As much as it was a cliche in horror&nbsp;
and adventure media, it seemed like the best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:15.600
course of action was to split into groups&nbsp;
of two or three and run in all directions.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:20.160
Without momentum, the clumps weren’t&nbsp;
especially fast, and given the sharp&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:23.940
turns and numerous crisscrossing&nbsp;
pathways of the Backrooms first level,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:28.320
the humans could - with a head start&nbsp;
- keep themselves at a safe distance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:33.360
if they used their brains and less&nbsp;
cumbersome limbs to maximum efficiency.

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:39.600
Dr. Hart chose her most trusted scientific&nbsp;
understudy, Dr. Whitaker as her retreat buddy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:44.520
and the two began to hurry down the many&nbsp;
hallways away from the clumps. If there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:49.740
was a way to survive these entities, even on&nbsp;
their home terrain, it would be through the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:55.620
superior intellect of the researchers. That is&nbsp;
what Dr. Hart believed in her doctor's heart.

00:05:55.620 --> 00:06:00.720
She and the others who followed her plan were&nbsp;
lucky that 096 had stopped zooming through the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:06.720
maze of the Backrooms first level. This was&nbsp;
because it realized that the entity or entities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:13.980
which were looking at it was not here in this&nbsp;
dimension. Or rather, this level of the Backrooms.

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:18.720
But that didn’t mean that whatever it was&nbsp;
could hide for long, especially not from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:25.860
SCP-096. The shy guy was capable of many things&nbsp;
when provoked by another being seeing its face,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:31.320
and among the most obvious was its&nbsp;
nigh-invulnerability and extreme speed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:38.640
Both of these factors would come into play as&nbsp;
SCP-096 attempted a bizarre and fascinating feat.

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:45.300
The shy guy’s entire body shivered, vibrating&nbsp;
in place at an even faster velocity than it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:50.340
had used to cross the infinite maze&nbsp;
in an instant moments prior. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:57.000
unorthodox psychics-straining movement&nbsp;
pattern made SCP-096 especially prone to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:01.620
no-clipping - which was the only reliable&nbsp;
way to navigate between levels of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:07.800
backrooms. The sustained vibration was highly&nbsp;
damaging to 096’s body, but it felt no pain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:13.080
and the broken bones and frayed muscles&nbsp;
were returned to normal instantaneously.

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:15.900
Furiously and with no further preparation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:22.200
SCP-096 no-clipped through the floor of the&nbsp;
maze and began to descend through the known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:27.840
levels of the backrooms towards the offending&nbsp;
entity that was still looking at its face.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:31.380
Down one level, then two, then three…

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:37.020
The pressure of maintaining this feat would more&nbsp;
than likely kill or incapacitate any other being,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:42.780
including many of SCP-096’s fellow&nbsp;
powerful anomalies. But that level&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:48.720
of endurance was what made SCP-096&nbsp;
so distinct and so unstoppable.

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:54.660
Four levels down. Five levels down.
As SCP-096 continued to descend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:58.860
the scattered personnel from the Foundation&nbsp;
were making their own discoveries about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:04.140
no-clipping throughout the Backrooms.&nbsp;
D-3461 had found himself in a strange&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:08.580
new level of the back rooms filled with&nbsp;
sewer pipes and swooping death moths.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:12.540
The rifle he had taken with him would&nbsp;
prove to be ample protection for now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:18.180
but he knew his ammunition wouldn’t be there&nbsp;
forever. Still, taking his chances sneaking around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:23.640
down here felt better than trying to go back&nbsp;
towards anyone who knew him from the foundation.

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:31.020
Like most D-Class, D-3461, formerly known as&nbsp;
Gene Beatty, was a hardened criminal through and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.020 --> 00:08:37.440
through, and had done unforgivable things prior&nbsp;
to his time contained by the SCP Foundation. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:43.740
didn’t want to go back, not to the Foundation,&nbsp;
not to prison, and not even to the real world.

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:48.480
Forget ‘em all. He thought. He would&nbsp;
survive in this hellish abyss known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:53.400
as Backrooms with only his malice and&nbsp;
sense of self-preservation to guide him.

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:57.600
Agent Cullen on the other hand, who was&nbsp;
accompanied by two of his surviving mobile&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:01.920
task force subordinates, was focused on&nbsp;
patrolling the yellow maze and searching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:07.080
for potential human survivors. If other people&nbsp;
had been no-clipping into the Backrooms for as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:12.360
long as the Foundation’s data suggested, it was&nbsp;
possible that enough of those unfortunates were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:17.820
able to carve out a life for themselves that&nbsp;
a sizable faction had formed over the years.

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:22.440
Such a group would always have a need for&nbsp;
armed assistance and well-trained soldiers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:26.880
so Cullen knew he could easily find&nbsp;
himself a place among them. From there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:29.880
he would do everything in his&nbsp;
power to muster resources,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:34.800
track down the scattered Foundation&nbsp;
personnel, and ultimately return home.

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:38.940
They have to be around here somewhere.&nbsp;
He told himself and his agents.&nbsp;

00:09:38.940 --> 00:09:45.240
Of all the now hopelessly lost researchers, it&nbsp;
seemed that Dr. Hart and Dr. Whitaker had made it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:51.120
the farthest into The Backrooms. They were both&nbsp;
now wandering in the Infinite Hotel - otherwise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:55.920
known as Level 5 - a sprawling labyrinth&nbsp;
of suites and lobbies that would rival the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.920 --> 00:10:01.440
finest establishments in the front rooms&nbsp;
of reality. That is, if it were not also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:05.460
full of the same kind of hostile entities&nbsp;
that were so common through the backrooms.

00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:08.400
Dr. Whitaker attempted to stay in high spirits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:15.420
however, making a sophomoric joke about needing&nbsp;
a “vacation from his vacation.” Dr. Hart groaned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:20.400
but on some level, she was grateful to have&nbsp;
her younger and more eccentric colleague close&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:25.620
by. Though he lacked common sense, he was&nbsp;
a prodigy at science, and more than that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:30.900
he was loyal. The two of them would need teamwork&nbsp;
and perseverance to keep going in this place,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:34.980
and through her mentorship of the young&nbsp;
man, the groundwork was already there.

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:39.180
He and I will manage somehow.&nbsp;
Dr. Hart affirmed in her mind.

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:44.520
Elsewhere, several levels down,&nbsp;
SCP-096 had arrived at the source&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:49.200
of the strange gaze that had been fixed&nbsp;
upon it. In level 11 of the backrooms:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:56.100
the city - which fittingly enough resembled a&nbsp;
modern human city of vast proportions - SCP-096&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.100 --> 00:11:02.580
was found locked onto the entity known&nbsp;
as Argos - entity 74 - an ancient eyeless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:07.440
humanoid whose vision was pervasive and&nbsp;
near-omniscient throughout the backrooms.

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:12.600
The cruel and judgemental being could observe the&nbsp;
sins of any sentient creature that entered the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:18.420
backrooms and would carry out a brutal punishment&nbsp;
accordingly. This was its routine behavior,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:26.580
and it didn’t single out SCP-096 anymore than it&nbsp;
did D-3461 - whose sins were much more severe in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:32.400
the eyes of Argos due to the ill intent behind&nbsp;
them. That is not to say that Argos saw the shy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:39.300
guy as innocent. Even out of perceived defense,&nbsp;
the amount of lives that SCP-096 had taken was,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:43.800
on principle, enough to call even&nbsp;
the most well-meaning being a sinner.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:48.660
A fight between Argos and the shy guy&nbsp;
was inevitable. Argos was accompanied&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:53.940
by several scores of spear-wielding warriors&nbsp;
in tactical gear - human explorers who had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:58.080
joined his cause. They would prove&nbsp;
to be little more than speed bumps,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:04.920
as 096 made skid marks out of them on its way&nbsp;
to pummel the everloving snot out of Argos.

00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:09.180
But Argos was not going to allow&nbsp;
the sacrifices of his “eyes” to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:14.100
in vain. The entity used the reach of&nbsp;
his spear to strike 096 at a distance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:20.040
impaling the creature in mid-run to the ground.&nbsp;
This held the shy guy for all but a moment before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:25.440
it moved its body up the spear and slammed&nbsp;
into Argos, throwing the two of them through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:30.660
a nearby building. Argos fought desperately to&nbsp;
remove his spear from his opponent's body as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:36.600
all the while 096 pounded him with punches that&nbsp;
could each reduce an automobile to scrap metal.

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:41.460
The two interlocked monsters tumbled&nbsp;
through wall after wall of the skyscraper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:46.080
taking the lives of several unlucky&nbsp;
human citizens in the process. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:51.300
Argos pried his spear free from 096, he&nbsp;
immediately jumped back several paces,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.300 --> 00:12:56.880
but once again, he had underestimated the&nbsp;
shy guy who was at his throat in seconds.

00:12:56.880 --> 00:13:03.000
Passersby on the street watched in horror&nbsp;
as 096 hurled Argos by the throat into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:07.740
skyscraper directly across from the one&nbsp;
they had been fighting in. Argos crashed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:12.960
through the glass of the windows and into&nbsp;
an office floor. One titanic leap from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:18.000
shy guy later, and 096 had joined&nbsp;
Argos on this new fighting stage.

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:22.740
Argos twirled his spear in a frenzied&nbsp;
display of combat prowess. If this thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:26.220
insisted on advancing towards him&nbsp;
with no regard for its well-being,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:32.460
it would have to go through his spear multiple&nbsp;
times over. But 096 was not the kind to let fear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.460 --> 00:13:37.440
stop it from advancing. It charged, taking&nbsp;
every attack Argos could dish out before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:42.600
pummeling him downward through several floors of&nbsp;
the building until they reached the ground level.

00:13:42.600 --> 00:13:49.380
SCP-096 could have taken far more punishment,&nbsp;
but Argos had reached his limit. The entity’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:56.040
spear fell from his hand as 096 continued to&nbsp;
hit harder and harder, over and over again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:56.040 --> 00:14:00.360
until Argos was as close to death as&nbsp;
an immortal backrooms entity could be.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:07.200
At the very least, he had been injured so severely&nbsp;
that his all-seeing gaze had become weakened.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:11.820
For the shy guy, this meant that Argos was&nbsp;
technically no longer looking at it. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:11.820 --> 00:14:16.440
became docile once more and wandered out&nbsp;
of the building into the streets. To its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:20.580
relief and to the relief of the nearby&nbsp;
entities, the facelings of this city&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:26.160
had no eyes and no interest in looking&nbsp;
at 096, preferring to continue their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:31.080
mindless pantomime of normative life.
Aren’t we all, in a cosmic sense?

00:14:31.080 --> 00:14:38.640
Regardless, SCP-096 walked through the streets&nbsp;
of the city with one goal: return home. But home&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:44.040
was far, far, away from where the shy guy was,&nbsp;
and the no-clipping maneuver that it performed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:48.840
earlier was not something that the anomaly&nbsp;
could muster the recklessness to do at all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:55.620
times. Only when its face was glimpsed did&nbsp;
SCP-096 possess its murderous determination.

00:14:55.620 --> 00:15:03.360
At the moment, SCP-096 was like a morning jogger,&nbsp;
traveling through Level 11 at a brisk pace and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:08.700
searching for a way out. This naturally led&nbsp;
the anomaly towards the suburban neighborhoods,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:13.260
which were themselves an entrance&nbsp;
to The Backrooms Level 9 - Suburbia.&nbsp;

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:18.180
It was here on the dark streets of the&nbsp;
limitless suburbs that 096 encountered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:22.500
a new nightmare - The Neighborhood&nbsp;
Watch. Comprised of a series of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:27.960
hostile entities resembling - in part -&nbsp;
human eyeballs, these ocular adversaries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:32.760
were known to patrol suburbia and keep&nbsp;
the peace… by eliminating all intruders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:38.580
of course. The floating watchers were capable of&nbsp;
shooting disintegration beams, while the towering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:43.980
striders possessed sinewy limbs that could&nbsp;
easily bash most entities into submission.

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:51.540
But… unfortunately for everyone involved -&nbsp;
they were giant eyeballs. One look from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:51.540 --> 00:15:57.840
Neighborhood Watch in the direction of SCP-096&nbsp;
and their fates were sealed. Being ogled by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.840 --> 00:16:03.480
humongous eyeballs was simply more than the shy&nbsp;
guy could take. With a primal screech, it ran&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:09.540
towards the oversized peepers with a massacre on&nbsp;
its mind. A few of the watchers had time to fire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:16.260
disintegration blasts, which slowed the approach&nbsp;
of SCP-096, but it was too little too late.

00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:22.260
SCP-096 smashed into the strider, knocking&nbsp;
it to the ground and delivering a crushing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:22.260 --> 00:16:28.200
blow to its pupil. Without missing a beat,&nbsp;
SCP-096 leaped into the air and smashed one&nbsp;&nbsp;

